    "incident_id": "notion-event-034",
    "outcome": "probable_cause",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "description": "Most likely cause: Cedar's Notion edit events reached trigger-worker, but the trigger was configured for page_created, so page_content_updated events did not match and were not delivered. This explains Cedar-local blocked operations and backlog without HTTP failures or a provider outage.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_b03e407bd73d",
          "ev_2743809125fc",
          "ev_8a3312eb9216",
          "ev_95640c90828a",
          "ev_c9919ec00db6"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [],
        "confidence": "high",
        "assumptions": [
          "The sampled Cedar request is representative of the missed edit executions during the incident window.",
          "The reported configuration change is not independently timestamped because no canonical config/audit record was supplied.",
          "The complaint that creates still arrive is unverified context; no canonical create-success record is present in-window."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "Alternative but less likely: a distinct edit-event subscription/setup issue exists. This is weakened because the failed Cedar edit event was already ingested by trigger-worker, so the observed failed execution does not require missing provider ingress.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_95640c90828a"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_b03e407bd73d",
          "ev_8a3312eb9216"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "This would require an additional configuration layer beyond the observed trigger event selector."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "Broader provider or platform failure is unlikely for the observed failure. The failing Cedar request reached trigger-worker with status 200, provider reachability is healthy, and Maple remained healthy in the same window.",
        "supporting_evidence": [],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_b03e407bd73d",
          "ev_2743809125fc",
          "ev_c9919ec00db6",
          "ev_cb557e970210"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "The supplied deployment evidence does not prove absence of a hidden trigger-worker change; it only fails to support that explanation."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "recommended_actions": [
      "Synthetic telemetry indicates the first priority is trigger_event_kind_mismatch_remediation: select the intended Notion update/edit trigger event for Cedar while preserving the existing connection, then verify with a newly generated edit.",
      "Collect missing canonical Cedar config/audit history for the incident window to confirm exactly what trigger configuration changed and when.",
      "If Cedar expects edits via a distinct subscription path, check the canonical setup/subscription records and subscribe_to_delivery_event only if that separate layer is actually required.",
      "Monitor backlog and blocked operations for Cedar after configuration review, and consider replay_after_recovery only for missed work if product semantics allow it; this has not been executed."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No canonical Cedar config/audit record was provided, so timing and exact nature of the reported trigger change remain unverified.",
      "No canonical in-window Cedar create-success record was supplied; the report does not prove creates continued succeeding during the sampled window.",
      "The reproduce tool is synthetic controlled telemetry, useful as a discriminating comparison but not proof of production change history.",
      "Empty partial dependency queries for tenant 'Cedar' are not evidence of absence and were not used to rule causes out."
    ]
  },
